---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../components/FinalCTA.astro';
import QuoteModal from '../components/QuoteModal.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="What is an alcohol interlock? — A plain-English guide | Interlock Alert"
  description="A short, plain-English guide to what alcohol interlocks are, how they work, who fits them, what they cost, and why UK fleets and households choose Interlock Alert."
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero hero--inner">
    <div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="wrap hero__grid hero__grid--narrow">
      <div class="hero__copy reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">A plain-English guide</span>
        <h1 class="display">
          What is an alcohol interlock? <span class="display__fade">And why are UK fleets fitting them?</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero__sub">
          An alcohol interlock is a pre-drive screening system — a practical way to enforce your driver alcohol policy at vehicle start, with breath testing, driver identification and an auditable trail of every event. Here's how it works, who fits one, and how to evaluate it without committing.
        </p>
        <div class="hero__cta">
          <button type="button" class="button button--primary button--lg" data-quote-open>
            <span class="button__label">Get a Free Quote</span>
            <svg class="icon-18" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-right"/></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT IS IT -->
  <section class="section section--band">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <header class="section__header reveal">
        <span class="section__eyebrow">The short answer</span>
        <h2 class="section__heading">A breath test wired into the ignition — and the audit trail to back it up.</h2>
        <p class="section__lede">An alcohol interlock is a small in-cab device that requires the driver to provide a breath sample before the engine will start. With Interlock Alert, that test is paired with an integrated camera that captures an image and short video clip of the person providing the sample, along with GPS, timestamp and BAC reading. A pass enables the ignition; a fail keeps the engine immobilised — and the entire event is logged to your portal in seconds.</p>
        <p class="section__lede">In the UK, interlocks are fitted privately — most often by fleet operators, businesses and HSE teams looking to move from policy on paper to enforcement on the dashboard. They are also fitted by households where drink driving is, for whatever reason, a decision best taken off the road entirely.</p>
      </header>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section__header reveal">
        <span class="section__eyebrow">How it works</span>
        <h2 class="section__heading">Four seconds between the key turn and a confirmed pass.</h2>
      </header>

      <ol class="steps" role="list">
        <li class="step reveal">
          <div class="step__num">01</div>
          <div class="step__icon-wrap"><svg class="icon-28" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-wind"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="step__title">Breath sample</h3>
          <p class="step__body">The driver blows into the handheld unit. With Interlock Alert, a front-facing camera captures a photo at the moment of the sample to verify identity.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step reveal reveal--delay-1">
          <div class="step__num">02</div>
          <div class="step__icon-wrap"><svg class="icon-28" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-activity"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="step__title">Result in seconds</h3>
          <p class="step__body">A fuel-cell sensor measures blood alcohol against a vehicle-specific threshold and returns a pass/fail in under three seconds.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step reveal reveal--delay-2">
          <div class="step__num">03</div>
          <div class="step__icon-wrap"><svg class="icon-28" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-key"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="step__title">Start or immobilise</h3>
          <p class="step__body">A pass enables the ignition. A fail keeps the engine fully immobilised at the ECU level — there is no second attempt and no rolling start.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step reveal reveal--delay-3">
          <div class="step__num">04</div>
          <div class="step__icon-wrap"><svg class="icon-28" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-file-log"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="step__title">Logged in real time</h3>
          <p class="step__body">Every test — pass or fail — is stamped with GPS, driver photo and timestamp, then synced to the Interlock Alert portal over 4G.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHO FITS IT -->
  <section class="section section--band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section__header reveal">
        <span class="section__eyebrow">Who fits one</span>
        <h2 class="section__heading">Where Interlock Alert is the right fit.</h2>
        <p class="section__lede section__lede--compact">Pre-drive alcohol screening is most often chosen by sectors with elevated safety risk, distributed mobile workforces, or formal compliance cultures — bus and coach operators, HGV and haulage, utilities and field service, waste and environmental services, construction fleets, and local authority operations. It is also fitted privately by households who want certainty.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="usecase-grid">
        <a class="usecase usecase--photo reveal" href="/use-cases/fleet-operators">
          <figure class="usecase__media">
            <img src="/images/fleet-operators.jpg" alt="Fleet of HGV trucks on a UK motorway" class="usecase__media-img" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </figure>
          <div class="usecase__content">
            <h3 class="usecase__title">Fleet operators</h3>
            <p class="usecase__body">O-licence holders, haulage and multi-drop operations who need a verified pass on record before the engine starts.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
        <a class="usecase usecase--photo reveal reveal--delay-1" href="/use-cases/trades-and-construction">
          <figure class="usecase__media">
            <img src="/images/site-vehicles.png" alt="Construction site vehicles and vans on a UK building site" class="usecase__media-img" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </figure>
          <div class="usecase__content">
            <h3 class="usecase__title">Trades &amp; construction</h3>
            <p class="usecase__body">Vans and site vehicles where one drink-drive incident can pull the contract, the insurance and the company name with it.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
        <a class="usecase usecase--photo reveal reveal--delay-2" href="/use-cases/company-vehicles">
          <figure class="usecase__media">
            <img src="/images/car-fleet.jpg" alt="Row of company fleet cars parked outside a UK office building" class="usecase__media-img" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </figure>
          <div class="usecase__content">
            <h3 class="usecase__title">Company vehicles</h3>
            <p class="usecase__body">Pool cars, grey fleet and assigned-driver vehicles where the brand on the bodywork is the company's liability.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
        <a class="usecase usecase--photo reveal reveal--delay-3" href="/use-cases/individuals-and-families">
          <figure class="usecase__media">
            <img src="/images/personal-car.jpg" alt="Individual driver beside a personal car on a residential street" class="usecase__media-img" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </figure>
          <div class="usecase__content">
            <h3 class="usecase__title">Individuals &amp; families</h3>
            <p class="usecase__body">Newly qualified drivers, those protecting a recovery, and households who want certainty on every key turn.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OBJECTIONS / FAQ DIRECT -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section__header reveal">
        <span class="section__eyebrow">Sensible questions</span>
        <h2 class="section__heading">The four questions every fleet asks before they fit one.</h2>
      </header>

      <div class="feature-grid feature-grid--threes">
        <article class="feature reveal">
          <div class="feature__icon"><svg class="icon-24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-camera"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="feature__title">"How do you know it was the driver who blew?"</h3>
          <p class="feature__body">The integrated camera captures a still image and short video clip at the moment of every breath test. The result is bound to the person who provided the sample — not anyone else in the cab.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature reveal reveal--delay-1">
          <div class="feature__icon"><svg class="icon-24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-shield-check"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="feature__title">"Doesn't this feel like surveillance?"</h3>
          <p class="feature__body">No. The camera engages only at the moment of the test, the driver knows it's there, and the policy is communicated upfront. It's policy enforcement, not in-cab monitoring.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature reveal reveal--delay-2">
          <div class="feature__icon"><svg class="icon-24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-lock"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="feature__title">"What happens if a driver fails?"</h3>
          <p class="feature__body">The engine is immobilised at the ECU level. The event is logged with image, GPS, BAC and timestamp, and an alert pushes to your nominated managers in seconds — so the next decision is yours, not the driver's.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature reveal">
          <div class="feature__icon"><svg class="icon-24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-wrench"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="feature__title">"How disruptive is the install?"</h3>
          <p class="feature__body">A single 90-minute appointment per vehicle, fitted at the ECU level by a certified UK auto-electrician. Warranty-safe, MOT-safe and fully reversible. For fleets, our engineers attend your depot.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature reveal reveal--delay-1">
          <div class="feature__icon"><svg class="icon-24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-monitor"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="feature__title">"Who can see the data?"</h3>
          <p class="feature__body">Only the people you nominate, with role-based access in the portal. UK-hosted, configurable retention, no third-party sharing or resale.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature reveal reveal--delay-2">
          <div class="feature__icon"><svg class="icon-24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-bolt"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="feature__title">"Will it work with our vehicles?"</h3>
          <p class="feature__body">Petrol, diesel, hybrid, EV — including HGVs, LCVs, PSVs, modern keyless platforms and CAN-bus systems. If it's road-legal in the UK, we install on it.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- COST + PILOT -->
  <section class="section section--band">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <header class="section__header reveal">
        <span class="section__eyebrow">What does it cost?</span>
        <h2 class="section__heading">Try it on a slice of your fleet first.</h2>
        <p class="section__lede">Interlock Alert is priced per device, per month — calibration, connectivity, software updates and UK-based support all included. There are no activation fees, no per-test charges, no multi-year lock-in. The exact monthly figure depends on the vehicle mix and the number of devices in your fleet.</p>
        <p class="section__lede">For most fleet customers the easiest path to a real number is a 30 to 60 day pilot. We agree the success criteria upfront — vehicles covered, drivers onboarded, manager feedback expected, failed-start events recorded — and you make the rollout decision at the end with your own data in hand.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="hero__cta" style="margin-top: 8px;">
        <button type="button" class="button button--primary button--lg" data-quote-open>
          <span class="button__label">Get a Free Quote</span>
          <svg class="icon-18" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-right"/></svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- INSTALLATION -->
  <section class="section section--band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="section__header reveal">
        <span class="section__eyebrow">Installation</span>
        <h2 class="section__heading">Fitted by certified engineers, in your region, usually within five working days.</h2>
      </header>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature reveal">
          <div class="feature__icon"><svg class="icon-24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-wrench"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="feature__title">Dealer-grade auto-electricians</h3>
          <p class="feature__body">Every install is carried out by a certified UK engineer working at the ECU level. Warranty-safe, MOT-safe, and discreet inside the cabin.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature reveal reveal--delay-1">
          <div class="feature__icon"><svg class="icon-24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-bolt"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="feature__title">All drivetrains supported</h3>
          <p class="feature__body">Petrol, diesel, hybrid and pure-electric vehicles, including modern keyless and CAN-bus platforms — including HGVs, LCVs and PSVs.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature reveal reveal--delay-2">
          <div class="feature__icon"><svg class="icon-24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-gb"/></svg></div>
          <h3 class="feature__title">UK-wide network</h3>
          <p class="feature__body">Engineers in every region. Most installations take a single appointment and are scheduled within five working days of accepting your quote.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHY INTERLOCK ALERT -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <header class="section__header section__header--center reveal">
        <span class="section__eyebrow">Why Interlock Alert</span>
        <h2 class="section__heading">The only UK interlock that's both camera-verified and cloud-connected.</h2>
        <p class="section__lede">Most interlocks on the UK market test breath, then leave you guessing. Interlock Alert pairs an identity-verifying driver camera with always-on 4G connectivity — so every test is provable, every result lands in your portal within seconds, and the audit trail is ready the moment a fleet manager, insurer or principal contractor asks for it. UK-built, UK-supported, with transparent monthly pricing and no lock-in.</p>
      </header>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FinalCTA
    useModal
    heading="Still have questions? Quickest way to a real answer is to ask one."
    body="Single vehicle or full fleet — share a few details and a UK-based engineer will come back with a tailored quote and an installation window, usually within one business day."
  />
  <QuoteModal />
</Layout>
